// std/integer.dag -- Integer types as carrier + algebra witness.
//
// T-Numeric-Construction Slice 3 pivots the default `Int` alias from the
// legacy 64-bit storage carrier to the honest construction-chain form.
// Authority chain:
//
//   - construction-chain layer 3.
//   - Q6 single-authority resolution: `type Int = AbelianGroup<GroupCompletion<Nat>>`,
//     not the rejected compact form `type Int = GroupCompletion<Nat>`.
//   - GroupCompletion<M> substrate-introduction (#1448, merged).
//   - Director ratifications on inbox #1288 (#4360232423 substrate-split,
//     #4362239705 Slice 3 alias-pivot dispatch).
//
// Construction-chain progression:
//
//   Magnitude → Nat = Semiring<Magnitude> → Int = AbelianGroup<GroupCompletion<Nat>> → ...
//
// `GroupCompletion<Nat>` is the **derived carrier** (opaque atom denoting
// the abelian-group carrier obtained from Nat via the Grothendieck
// construction). `AbelianGroup<T>` is the standard algebra witness over
// that carrier — `T = GroupCompletion<Nat>` types `inverse: fn(GroupCompletion<Nat>) -> GroupCompletion<Nat>`,
// which is honest by construction (every element of the group-completion
// carrier has an additive inverse).
//
// Fixed-width rows (`Int8`..`Int128`, `UInt8`..`UInt128`) are **width
// refinements** of the abstract carriers `Int` / `UInt` via
// `Compose<Algebra, MachineWidth<N>>` with literal-Nat `N` in slot-2 for every
// fixed width including 8-bit (`MachineWidth<8>`), matching parser-lowered
// `Int<8>` / `UInt<8>` / `Nat<8>` (R3 gate #60 Slice Z; DESIGN.md §3 single
// slot-2 authority). Gate #19 `numeric_aliases_align_to_refinements` — not
// parallel `OrderedRing<Word*>` / `Semiring<Word*>` substrate. Grounding still
// maps each pair to the same Rust `i*` / `u*` primitives as before (`Byte` at
// `dsl/std/bit.dag` remains the nominal 8-bit **value** carrier for primitives;
// machine-width slot-2 is indexed by literal `8`, not `Byte`).
//
// Signed/unsigned distinction comes from the algebra (legacy fixed-width rows):
//   OrderedRing has negate (signed arithmetic — additive inverse)
//   Semiring has no negate (unsigned — only add and mul)

module std.integer

import std.algebra { AbelianGroup, GroupCompletion }
import std.nat { Nat }
import std.machine_constraints { Compose, MachineWidth, PointerWidth }

// Signed integers: abstract `Int` × machine width (refinement-shaped Compose).
type Int8 = Compose<Int, MachineWidth<8>>
type Int16 = Compose<Int, MachineWidth<16>>
type Int32 = Compose<Int, MachineWidth<32>>
type Int64 = Compose<Int, MachineWidth<64>>
type Int128 = Compose<Int, MachineWidth<128>>

// Unsigned integers: abstract `UInt` (= Nat) × machine width.
type UInt8 = Compose<UInt, MachineWidth<8>>
type UInt16 = Compose<UInt, MachineWidth<16>>
type UInt32 = Compose<UInt, MachineWidth<32>>
type UInt64 = Compose<UInt, MachineWidth<64>>
type UInt128 = Compose<UInt, MachineWidth<128>>

// S9 Phase-1 step 3 emission entries — parametric `Compose<Algebra, MachineConstraint>`
// instantiations per Q-MachineConstraint sub-decision 2 RATIFIED at gunbc#828
// #issuecomment-4385530115 (NOT AlgebraMachineProduct table rows).
//
// Slot-1 spelling = fully-applied algebraic-concept name (`Int` =
// `AbelianGroup<GroupCompletion<Nat>>` per #1466 Q6 audit; `UInt` = `Nat`
// per #1818 / single-authority framing) — NOT bare witness shape (Q-MC sub-decision
// 3 critical correction: witness shape doesn't go in slot-1; the named
// concept does).
//
// Slot-2 spelling = `MachineWidth<N>` literal-Nat phantom index (gate #60 Slice Z),
// including `N = 8` for the 8-bit rows — sibling to `MachineWidth<PointerWidth>` on
// `IntPlatform` / `UIntPlatform` below (opaque / target-resolved inner tokens).

// Default aliases.
//
// T-Numeric-Construction Slice 3 alias-pivot.
//
// `Int` is the abstract integer algebra: an `AbelianGroup` over the
// derived `GroupCompletion<Nat>` carrier. `GroupCompletion<Nat>` (from
// `std.algebra`) is the opaque atom denoting "the abelian-group carrier
// derived from Nat via the Grothendieck construction"; `AbelianGroup<T>`
// over that carrier is the standard algebra witness. This is the canonical
// Q6 single-authority form; the compact
// alternative `type Int = GroupCompletion<Nat>` was explicitly rejected.
//
// Fixed-width `Int8`..`Int128` names refine this abstract `Int` via Compose
// (see above); only this declaration is the unconstrained abstract carrier.
//
// `UInt` is the abstract unsigned-integer algebra. Per the design-doc
// authority `UInt IS Nat`, the faithful pivot is the direct alias —
// `Nat` is already `CommutativeSemiring<Magnitude>` (additive monoid +
// multiplicative monoid + distribution + commutativity on both), which
// IS the unsigned-integer algebra surface. Wrapping `Nat` in
// `CommutativeMonoid<Nat>` (or `Monoid<Nat>`) would project out the
// multiplicative structure and the multiplicative identity `1`,
// violating facts-flow-forward (DESIGN.md §3 single authority) — the substrate cannot structurally
// name "the additive monoid projection of Nat" without dropping
// Nat's other monoid. The brief's `CommutativeMonoid<Nat>` shorthand
// is anemic for the same reason `Int = AbelianGroup<Nat>` would be
// unfaithful: it discards substrate facts already established at the
// Nat layer.
//
// (Asymmetry with `Int` is structural: `Int` requires additive
// inverses that Nat lacks, so the explicit `GroupCompletion<Nat>`
// carrier is necessary to introduce them honestly. `UInt` requires no
// new operations beyond what Nat already carries, so no new carrier
// or projection is needed — the alias IS the algebra.)
//
// Fixed-width `UInt8`..`UInt128` refine this carrier via Compose (see above).
type Int = AbelianGroup<GroupCompletion<Nat>>
type UInt = Nat

// IntPlatform / UIntPlatform — pointer-width-sized integer substrate concepts.
//
// Per Director Q1+Q2+Q3+Q4 RATIFIED at gunbc#1739 #issuecomment-4393248961
// (2026-05-07) + inner-token rename `Platform` → `PointerWidth` RATIFIED
// at gunbc#828 #issuecomment-4393616097. Outer carrier names
// `IntPlatform`/`UIntPlatform` stay verbatim (Q1 RATIFIED). Inner substrate
// token is `PointerWidth` to avoid collision with pre-existing
// `Platform = Linux | Macos | Windows` (OS-identity axis) at
// `dsl/std/types.dag:356`; per reason-not-label, pointer-width
// is the structural reason and OS-identity vs pointer-width are
// orthogonal axes (32-bit Linux vs 64-bit Linux are different pointer
// widths but same OS).
//
// Composition per Q-MachineConstraint-Carrier sub-decision 3
// (gunbc#828 #issuecomment-4385530115) extended with substrate token
// `PointerWidth` per Q3 ratification (substrate-concept layer, NOT target-
// only) — `MachineWidth<PointerWidth>` resolves at Grounding-emit time
// per target spec; substrate stays target-agnostic.
//
// Direct consumer: the target integer-inhabitance rows for `isize`
// (kernel_integer = IntPlatform) and `usize` (kernel_integer = UIntPlatform)
// with `bound: PlatformDependentFact`.
// Targets without native pointer-sized integers (Python's arbitrary-
// precision `int`, etc.) handle ground-time projection via target-
// conditioned **lowering** — substrate stays clean (Grounding-lane work).
//
// Decomposition (DESIGN.md §2): N/A — type aliases over existing `Compose<...>` carrier;
// no new sum types or coproducts introduced here.
type IntPlatform  = Compose<Int,  MachineWidth<PointerWidth>>
type UIntPlatform = Compose<UInt, MachineWidth<PointerWidth>>

// Nat-alignment refinements (S9 Slice 2 / Slice 2.5 / Phase-4).
//
// NonNegativeInt formerly lived in dsl/std/types.dag refining Int with a
// non-negative range predicate. Slice 2 Nat-alignment migrates the
// algebra-side carrier to Nat: non-negativity is structural to Nat by
// construction (the canonical natural-number carrier), not a refinement
// over Int. Refining Int for non-negativity projects out Nat's structural
// property — the same modeling fault Codex's BLOCKING review on PR #1818
// caught for UInt as a CommutativeMonoid wrap of Nat. Declared here (not
// in std.types) because this module imports std.nat directly; locating in
// std.types would require an std.types to std.nat import edge that
// triggers a circular-dependency false-positive during transitive load of
// test fixtures via std.render chains.
//
// PositiveInt migrates to Nat-where-gt_zero per S9 Slice 2.5 (Path 3
// RATIFIED at gunbc#828 issuecomment-4390333451). The gt_zero primitive
// IS the reason for "Nat without zero" / "Nat above structural bound"
// (Director Option 2 ratification at gunbc#828 issuecomment-4390199218);
// the prior range(min: 1) over Int was a misleading label that treated
// Nat's lower-bound = 0 as a contingent rather than structural fact.
// gt_zero is enrolled in the lowerer's predicate registry, which
// retired the prior PB-1 file-path special case.
type NonNegativeInt = Nat
type PositiveInt    = Nat where gt_zero

// ─── Diagnostic enumeration order (Modeling problem 4; slice 2) ─────────────
//
// **Substrate-declared ordering authority** for diagnostic enumeration (narrow→wide).
// Not emission policy — fail-closed UX only. The ordered rows are keyed by
// `DeclarationRef`, which is not loaded in the dsl-only std bootstrap seed.
//
// **Dissolution:** when typed `width_bits` (or equivalent) lands on word carriers
// (`dsl/std/bit.dag`), derive order from carriers and remove these lists.
